    description: "Found by the 2026-11-15 review of the stable-id items (reports and fixtures: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026). Re-run by hand the same day at dev e2b6ab8096, analyzer 9.2.0.\n\nDEFECT. REPRO, ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/work/new/cpp/src/a.hpp:\n\n    struct Mgr {};\n    struct Impl {\n      Impl() { Init(); }\n      void Init() { helper(); }\n      template <typename M>\n      void Init(M *m) { helper(); }\n      void helper() {}\n    };\n\n`hypergumbo run` emits `Impl` (function, line 3) -> `Init` (function, line 6): the constructor's zero-argument call\nis bound to the one-parameter template. `Impl::Init` (method, line 4), the overload the call selects, gets no edge\nfrom the constructor.\n\nSeen first on a real header: sherpa-onnx d7526c8, keyword-spotter-transducer-impl.h, line 77 `InitKeywords();` in\nthe in-class constructor binds the template at line 319, not the zero-argument overload at line 294.\n\nCAUSE, as far as checked. Both ends are the two shapes of WI-rugin-jopak-muhuv-fihod-tojuz-banod-gizid-dusur: the in-class constructor and the member template\nare emitted as free `function`s with bare names (`Impl`, `Init`), while the plain member is `method Impl::Init`.\nThe call from one bare-named function finds the other bare-named function by name; the parameter count (0 against\n1) does not exclude it. WI-hilum-robok-dokop-jofuj-losof-navuj-zitof-nurav (done) added an arity check for overloaded names; it did not apply here.\n\nDEPENDS ON WI-rugin-jopak-muhuv-fihod-tojuz-banod-gizid-dusur: once the constructor and the template are methods of Impl, this call has two same-name member\ncandidates of different arity. This item is then the check that the zero-argument one is chosen. WI-jutur-tonul-buloj-toson-mijum-jozot-havok-pipih covers\nsame-ARITY overloads, which is a different case.\n\nACCEPTANCE. On the fixture the constructor's edge goes to the zero-argument Init at line 4 and not to the template.\n\nNOT CHECKED: whether the arity check is skipped because the candidate is a template, or because caller and\ncandidate are both of kind function; a default argument on the template's parameter."  # 9bc7
    fields: {}  # 9bc7
