  message: "Fixed in PR #2200. Re-ran the filed fixture and the sherpa-onnx header it came from: the zero-argument call inside the in-class constructor bound the one-parameter member template on dev (fixture line 6; header line 319) and binds the zero-argument `Init` now (line 4; line 294). Overloads and `new` choose by arity. RULE ADDED AND ITS LIMIT: on an arity tie with exactly one non-template candidate, that candidate is the pick and the record STAYS ambiguous. At keyword-spotter-transducer-impl.h:98 (`InitKeywords(mgr)` with a `Manager*`) the pick is therefore the `std::istream&` overload at line 283, which is the wrong one; dev picked the template at line 319. The record says ambiguous in both. Argument shapes are WI-jutur-tonul-buloj-toson-mijum-jozot-havok-pipih's scope; the reachability consequence is filed with the C++ residual. NOT CHECKED: a template with a default argument. Repro record (both arms, commands and copied outputs): ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr2/tracker/repros.md; per-package detail: pr2/STATUS.md; churn: pr2/final_measure.txt."  # 522f
